{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>One lamb, and one ewe lamb, and one ram.</b> Three things, to permit three prohibitions of the nazirite; and corresponding to them, within the ram itself there are three categories of eating: for the altar, for the priest, and for the owners." "<b>And one ram, perfect, for shelamim.</b> Rejoicing over the fact that he completed what he had vowed. And this ram requires semikhah, and tenufah of the breast and thigh, and the eimurim, and the boiled foreleg."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:43.549087192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}